<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106067" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλο-φόρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>carrying a blind
			person</i>:—in <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				<u>Syrinx</u>
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				15.21
			</span></i>) said by Sch.to be 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πηροφόρος</span>
			, <i>carrying a scrip</i> or <i>wallet</i>; jestingly, as
			if, because <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηρός</span> means
			<i>blind,</i> therefore <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλή</span> is 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηρά
				ʽπήρἀ.</span>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
